<title>SPAIN: Telefonica retail demand nears 1 mln bids.</title>
<headline>Telefonica retail demand nears 1 mln bids.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Spain's Telefonica Juan Villalonga said on Thursday that almost one million people have ordered shares in the firm's current privatisation.</p>
<p>The government is selling its last 20.9 percent stake in the domestic telephone operator, of which half is being offered to small shareholders in Spain.</p>
<p>&quot;As of yesterday we had more than 990,000 demands,&quot; Villalonga said in an interview on Spanish radio.</p>
<p>On Wednesday Telefonica announced 1996 net profit of 160.03 billion pesetas, up 20.1 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
